From 6291e083a98e54a3240dc305e46f0ab68902247b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:50:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] StaticRecomp: a runtime cycle budget for generated code

From Piconet's RecompCore (StaticRecompCore_Sync/Run/Hooks): a module
built with DOLRECOMP_BUDGET_CYCLES=runtime reads CPUState.cycle_budget
at its calls and loop heads instead of leaving every 256 cycles.
- BeginDispatchBudget: before a dispatch, the budget is the downcount
  left to Dolphin's next event (256 after a wait loop, m_wait_streak).
- FlushDispatchCharge / RefreshDispatchBudget: a hardware access first
  charges the cycles run so far to Dolphin's clock (downcount, timebase),
  then sets the budget again (the access may schedule an earlier event).
- A dispatch whose cycles a hardware access already charged costs no
  extra cycle.
- AdvanceGuestTimebase counts the charge as ticks with the CPU clock
  factor (Core.Overclock); unchanged at 1.
SRNP_NO_HOOK_FLUSH=1 turns the flush off, for comparisons.

Sonic Riders, demo race, 1800 frames: with the step-A module (fixed
budget of 256) 169.8 frames/s (B1: 174.8-176.5, within the noise);
_Main.rel's BSS at the pause identical; lockstep 600 frames: the same
kinds of divergences as without it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
